ant to tuck this corner  inside just like that fold this flap  down and then we make another crease so  now you should have a paper that looks  something like this and if you made  really good creases when you were  tucking the corners in then you should  see a faint line that runs vertically  down the middle of this diamond so what  we want to do is we want to take the  corner of this paper the first layer and  we're going to fold it so that this edge  here is on that line that runs  vertically  so you should have something that looks  like that and you want to do that for  the remaining three flaps so take this  one hold it up there and make a crease  flip it over and do the same for these  two all right this next fold that I'm  going to show you which is known as the  petal fold is one of the trickiest folds  of making the crane what we want to do  is we want to first unfold these folds  which we just made and we want to  flatten it out so it is again in a  diamond shape flip it over and do the  same for this side now we want to do is  we want to take this corner here this  first layer and we want to lift it up  just like this and what we're going to  do is we're going to kind of pull on it  until these corners start to tuck in  word so once they start to tuck inward  what you want to do is you want to take  it and you want to kind of crease it  along that line which we previously made  and then you want to flatten it out just  like that so that's called the petal  fold and as you'll see you kind of have  this petal structure so you want to  flatten it out and you're going to do  the same for the other side take this  corner lift it up as you'll see the  paper might not want to fold there so  what you got to do is you take your  thumb and you just just pop it outward  so that these corner pieces can tuck  inward toward the center of the diamond  okay so then you should be able to kind  of flatten it down and fold these corner  pieces directly into the center and 